{"name":"Aloha Sunset","hex":"#e9aa91","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aloha","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Good wishes, love, compassion, peacefulness and affection. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An utterance of aloha (see Interjection, below)."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Expressing good wishes when greeting or parting from someone; hello; goodbye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aloha"},{"term":"sunset","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The moment each evening when the sun disappears below the western horizon.","The changes in color of the sky before and after sunset."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunset"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aloha","blocks":[{"text":"Aloha is the Hawaiian word for love, affection, peace, compassion, and mercy. It can also be used to welcome or bid farewell to someone. It has a deeper cultural and spiritual significance for native Hawaiians, who use the term to define a force that holds together existence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG/330px-Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aloha","wikidata":"Q508880"},{"title":"Sunset","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset is the disappearance of the Sun at the end of the Sun path, below the horizon of the Earth due to its rotation. As viewed from everywhere on Earth, it is a phenomenon that happens approximately once every 24 hours, except in areas close to the poles. The equinox Sun sets due west at the moment of both the spring and autumn equinoxes. As viewed from the Northern Hemisphere, the Sun sets to the northwest in the spring and summer, and to the southwest in the autumn and winter; these seasons are reversed for the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg/330px-Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset","wikidata":"Q166564"},{"title":"Sunset (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color sunset is a pale tint of orange. It is a representation of the average color of clouds when the sunlight from a sunset is reflected from them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Sunset_2007-1.jpg/330px-Sunset_2007-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_(color)","wikidata":"Q11696368"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG/500px-Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG/1280px-Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG/500px-Flowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowers arranged to make the word aloha","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlowers_arranged_to_ALOHA%2C_Hilo%2C_Hawaii.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/1991_Hawaii_license_plate_MNG_728.jpg/330px-1991_Hawaii_license_plate_MNG_728.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/1991_Hawaii_license_plate_MNG_728.jpg/330px-